            {
                "entry_id": "1ca4427e-bcc1-3b99-96e8-72156dc5741d",
                "word": "downward",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "43509474-2c5f-3b54-babe-1a1688eee4e4",
                        "entry_id": "1ca4427e-bcc1-3b99-96e8-72156dc5741d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Toward a lower level, whether in physical space, in a hierarchy, or in amount or value."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fed3eb58-4a11-4c70-9e45-6548b7b16520",
                                "sense_id": "43509474-2c5f-3b54-babe-1a1688eee4e4",
                                "text": "His position in society moved ever downward."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "001eff40-9fc5-4463-9a25-521e2b6c2cbf",
                                "sense_id": "43509474-2c5f-3b54-babe-1a1688eee4e4",
                                "text": "The natural disasters put downward pressure on the creditworthiness of the nation’s insurance groups."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d9786ef-ec46-4319-a612-d171d430b361",
                                "sense_id": "43509474-2c5f-3b54-babe-1a1688eee4e4",
                                "text": "[A] ring the county wears, / That downward hath succeeded in his house / From son to son, some four or five descents"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20d46a97-d3e2-4f76-bb95-777972259162",
                                "sense_id": "43509474-2c5f-3b54-babe-1a1688eee4e4",
                                "text": "They call her Daffadill: / Whoſe preſence as ſhe went along, / The prety flowers did greet, / As though their heads they downward bent, / With homage to her feete."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2bc73528-dd44-4a44-a1c2-54000975a8c5",
                                "sense_id": "43509474-2c5f-3b54-babe-1a1688eee4e4",
                                "text": "Novv you muſt bee ſure […] to carry the point or top of the Rod dovvnevvard; by vvhich meanes the ſhadovv of your ſelfe, and Rod too vvill be the leaſt offenſive to the Fiſh, for the ſight of any ſhadovv amazes the fiſh, and ſpoiles your ſport, of vvhich you muſt take a great care."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2521de06-8ac9-49de-9f25-4b586f54438d",
                                "sense_id": "43509474-2c5f-3b54-babe-1a1688eee4e4",
                                "text": "[T]heir Sight was so directed downward, that they did not readily see Objects that were above them […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26ce3b16-9a54-47d1-9b64-71bca321b6f7",
                                "sense_id": "43509474-2c5f-3b54-babe-1a1688eee4e4",
                                "text": "Down, downward they went, and yet further down—their descent at each step seeming to outmeasure their advance."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ae556a4c-49d2-36e2-aa03-210b6c54126f",
                        "entry_id": "1ca4427e-bcc1-3b99-96e8-72156dc5741d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "At a lower level."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "667fbe48-e512-4f6e-8b6a-2a80774ebb1c",
                                "sense_id": "ae556a4c-49d2-36e2-aa03-210b6c54126f",
                                "text": "Dagon his Name, Sea Monster, upward Man / And downward Fish […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "58c1aa76-16a3-3de0-87d7-7842c9c20bfc",
                        "entry_id": "1ca4427e-bcc1-3b99-96e8-72156dc5741d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Southward."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebd31bc1-adba-44ec-b9ab-c7fccd510155",
                                "sense_id": "58c1aa76-16a3-3de0-87d7-7842c9c20bfc",
                                "text": "If we turn to the New World, we find that among the American Indians, from the Eskimo of Alaska downward to Brazil and still farther south, homosexual customs have been very frequently observed."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "95cc0745-4193-4b57-80d9-96d9687d3756",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ca4427e-bcc1-3b99-96e8-72156dc5741d",
                        "source_sense_description": "toward a lower level",
                        "target_lang_word": "abwärts",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "abwärts",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8bcd39c0-e559-3974-babc-b02c9fcc73bc",
                                        "entry_id": "61700410-4c3b-3769-9a3c-5edb9c4587f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "nach unten"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e2adcf6-5d51-448a-aae9-b81dc950b0a8",
                                                "sense_id": "8bcd39c0-e559-3974-babc-b02c9fcc73bc",
                                                "text": "Laut Human Rights Watch in China wurden ihm die Halswirbelknochen gebrochen, so dass er nun von den Schultern abwärts gelähmt ist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95b03334-cb41-4a18-9816-d08873d5819e",
                                                "sense_id": "8bcd39c0-e559-3974-babc-b02c9fcc73bc",
                                                "text": "Von der Gruppenleiterin an abwärts gibt es keinen pauschalierten Fahrkostenzuschuss."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27501edc-ca41-48a9-b26d-20a56b4b5917",
                                                "sense_id": "8bcd39c0-e559-3974-babc-b02c9fcc73bc",
                                                "text": "Der Aufzug fährt jetzt abwärts. Wenn Sie in die andere Richtung wollen, müssen Sie warten, bis er wieder vorbeikommt."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
